er]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135368298.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Domena Diesing took a significant step by investing her grandmother's legacy to safeguard 140 acres of Lasqueti Island, Canada. By teaming up with the BC Parks Foundation, she secured a permanent conservation status for the land, enhancing a vast connected reserve now exceeding 1,000 acres in the Salish Sea. This project commemorates Alfred Gaensbauer’s enduring dedication to environmental preservation, ensuring a legacy of rich coastal habitats for generations to come.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-woman-used-her-grandmothers-inheritance-to-buy-into-a-canadian-island-property-in-1981-45-years-later-she-and-her-partner-have-protected-140-acres-of-forest-while-keeping-their-20-acre-homestead/articleshow/135368298.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-woman-used-her-grandmothers-inheritance-to-buy-into-a-canadian-island-property-in-1981-45-years-later-she-and-her-partner-have-protected-140-acres-of-forest-while-keeping-their-20-acre-homestead/articleshow/135368298.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T21:33:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135369136,imgsize-1640089.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian national jailed for 8 years in US over laundering case targeting elderly people; ordered to pay $2.4m to victims]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135368796.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-national-jailed-for-8-years-in-us-over-laundering-case-targeting-elderly-people-ordered-to-pay-2-4m-to-victims/articleshow/135368796.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-national-jailed-for-8-years-in-us-over-laundering-case-targeting-elderly-people-ordered-to-pay-2-4m-to-victims/articleshow/135368796.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T21:30:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135369059,imgsize-63976.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Penn's Cave, family-owned since 1908, goes up for sale for $34 million after 118 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135367947.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Campbell family has put Penn's Cave and Wildlife Park in Centre Hall up for sale, ending a remarkable 118-year legacy. With a listing price of $34 million, this expansive estate includes an impressive limestone cave system, a vibrant wildlife park, and a private airport. As the sale process begins, state officials in Pennsylvania are looking into potential conservation strategies, with the family promising a smooth transition of current operations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-family-has-owned-penns-cave-since-1908-and-expanded-its-land-to-protect-its-water-118-years-later-the-1400-acre-attraction-with-a-cavern-wildlife-park-and-airport-is-seeking-a-new-owner/articleshow/135367947.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-pennsylvania-family-has-owned-penns-cave-since-1908-and-expanded-its-land-to-protect-its-water-118-years-later-the-1400-acre-attraction-with-a-cavern-wildlife-park-and-airport-is-seeking-a-new-owner/articleshow/135367947.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T20:57:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135368215,imgsize-1448634.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Martha Washington’s 1760 Letter About Daughter’s Illness Sells for $47,500, Joins Library of Congress]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135364786.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A personal letter from Martha Washington, describing her daughter's recovery, has found a new home at the Library of Congress. This 1760 correspondence, directed to Margaret Green, sheds light on Martha's motherhood journey and is the first handwritten piece by her in the library's archives. Its acquisition underscores women's vital roles during colonial America, adding depth alongside Mary Todd Lincoln's letters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-letter-martha-washington-wrote-in-1760-about-her-four-year-old-daughters-illness-sold-for-47500-the-library-of-congress-has-acquired-the-rare-document-its-first-original-letter-in-marthas-own-handwriting/articleshow/135364786.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-letter-martha-washington-wrote-in-1760-about-her-four-year-old-daughters-illness-sold-for-47500-the-library-of-congress-has-acquired-the-rare-document-its-first-original-letter-in-marthas-own-handwriting/articleshow/135364786.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T20:55:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135364887,imgsize-27928.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Dolly Parton's free book programme sees 950 new sign-ups and $150,000 in donations after her death]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135361347.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In the wake of Dolly Parton's passing, the Imagination Library saw a remarkable increase in registrations. In August alone, Knox County welcomed nearly 950 new children to the program. Additionally, over $150,000 was generated through a fundraising initiative to bolster the library's mission. Established in 1995, this program ensures that young readers receive free books every month until the age of five, proudly distributing over four million books to date.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dolly-parton-started-giving-free-books-to-children-31-years-ago-a-new-october-29-report-says-her-knox-county-programme-attracted-nearly-950-sign-ups-in-august-and-raised-over-150000-following-her-death/articleshow/135361347.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/dolly-parton-started-giving-free-books-to-children-31-years-ago-a-new-october-29-report-says-her-knox-county-programme-attracted-nearly-950-sign-ups-in-august-and-raised-over-150000-following-her-death/articleshow/135361347.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T18:24:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135362764,imgsize-1684051.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Elon Musk clarifies how often he meets his 13 children and how many staffs are involved in the entire process]]></title><description><![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/elon-musk-clarifies-how-often-he-meets-his-13-children-and-how-many-staffs-are-involved-in-the-entire-process/articleshow/135366780.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/elon-musk-clarifies-how-often-he-meets-his-13-children-and-how-many-staffs-are-involved-in-the-entire-process/articleshow/135366780.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-30T20:17:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135366876,imgsize-13412.cms"/></item></channel></rss>